    "body": "## Description\n\n`dataset_kwargs` on a dataset config is documented as \"passed to the dataset loading function `get_custom_dataset`\", and each routed source has its own `dataset_kwargs` for \"this source's loader\". `get_custom_dataset` only merged them into the `RDataset` built for the data service. When the dataset is loaded in process, which happens with the SPMD launchers (local/ray/slurm set `AREAL_SPMD_MODE=1`) or with `scheduling_spec=None`, only the call kwargs reached `_get_custom_dataset`, so the configured kwargs were silently dropped, including per-source kwargs of a routed mixture (`get_routed_dataset` merges them into the source config).\n\nRepro (AREAL_SPMD_MODE=1, `_get_custom_dataset` patched to record its kwargs):\n\n```python\ncfg = TrainDatasetConfig(path=\"swe-data.jsonl\", type=\"sft\", dataset_kwargs={\"num_proc\": 4})\nget_custom_dataset(split=\"train\", dataset_config=cfg)\n# before: num_proc missing from the loader kwargs; after: num_proc=4\n```\n\nThis PR merges the configured kwargs once, before the remote/local branch, and passes them on both paths. Call kwargs still take precedence, as they already did for the remote path.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nNone found (searched open and closed issues and PRs).\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix\n- [ ] ✨ New feature\n- [ ] 💥 Breaking change\n- [ ] 📝 Documentation update\n- [ ] ♻️ Refactoring\n- [ ] ⚡ Performance improvement\n- [ ] ✅ Test coverage improvement\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read the\n  [Contributing Guide](https://github.com/areal-project/community/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [ ] Pre-commit hooks pass (`pre-commit run --all-files`). I ran ruff (v0.14.9) lint and format on the changed files only.\n- [x] Relevant tests pass; new tests added for new functionality\n- [ ] Documentation updated (if applicable; built with `./docs/build_all.sh`)\n- [x] Branch is up to date with `main`\n- [ ] Self-reviewed via `/review-pr` command\n- [ ] This PR was created by a coding agent via `/create-pr`\n- [ ] This PR is a breaking change\n\n**Breaking Change Details (if applicable):**\n\nN/A\n\n## Additional Context\n\nThe new test (SPMD mode, and single-controller with `scheduling_spec=None`) fails on current `main` with `KeyError: 'num_proc'` and passes with this change. `tests/infra/data_service/test_trainer_compat.py`, `tests/test_mopd_dataset.py` and `tests/test_dataset_swe_path_dispatch.py` pass (CPU only).\n\nAI use: I used an AI coding assistant (Claude Code) while writing the fix and tests; I reviewed the changes and ran the checks listed above.\n",
